---
// The privacy policy. The long text is Markdown in src/content/pages/privacy.md. The parts
// that depend on facts the company has not given yet are built here, from the same source
// as the imprint (src/lib/legal.ts), so they update themselves and never claim more than
// is set:
//   - the draft note, shown until the admin sets `reviewed: true` in privacy.md
//   - who the controller is: the company's details once they are in imprint.md
//   - how to reach us about your data: WhatsApp and e-mail once they are set; the quiz always
//   - "When you visit the website", the Meta Pixel paragraph (only while a Meta Pixel id is set
//     in site.json) and the advertisers' conversion tags sentence (only while a thank-you page
//     code is set); with either, the site has a cookie banner (CookieBanner.astro)
import { getEntry, render } from 'astro:content';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { formatDay, getLegalFacts, listText, lowerFirst } from '../lib/legal';
import { getSite } from '../lib/texts';
import { metaPixelId, thanksCode } from '../scripts/site-values.js';

const entry = await getEntry('pages', 'privacy');
if (!entry) throw new Error('src/content/pages/privacy.md is missing');
const { Content } = await render(entry);
const { missing, fact, email, whatsapp } = await getLegalFacts();
const asOf = formatDay(entry.data.updated);
const draft = entry.data.reviewed !== true;

const name = fact('companyName');
const form = fact('legalForm');
const office = fact('address');
const number = fact('enterpriseNumber');
const one = missing.length === 1;
const missingText = listText(missing.map(lowerFirst));
const direct = Boolean(whatsapp || email);
const site = await getSite();
const pixel = Boolean(metaPixelId(site.tracking.metaPixelId));
const tags = Boolean(thanksCode(site.tracking.thanksCode));
const consent = pixel || tags;
---

<LegalPage entry={entry}>
  {draft && (
    <p>
      <strong>A note before you read.</strong> This policy is a draft. It describes accurately how this website handles your
      data as of {asOf}, and it is waiting for {missing.length > 0 ? 'the company’s legal details and its own review' : 'the company’s own review'}.
      Until then, the ways to reach us about your data are listed below, under “How to reach us about your data”.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  {name ? (
    <p>
      The controller of your personal data under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is {name}{form && `, ${form}`}
      {office && `, with its registered office at ${office}`}{number && `, enterprise number ${number}`}.
      {missing.length > 0 && ` As of ${asOf}, its ${missingText} ${one ? 'is' : 'are'} not yet published on this site.`}
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      This website is run by a company established in Belgium, which is the controller of your personal data under the EU
      General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). As of {asOf}, its {missingText} {one ? 'is' : 'are'} not yet published
      on this site. {one ? 'It' : 'They'} will be added to this policy and to the imprint as soon as the company has
      confirmed {one ? 'it' : 'them'}.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>How to reach us about your data</h2>
  <p>
    For anything about your data, for example to ask what we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, or to
    withdraw your consent:
  </p>
  <ul>
    {whatsapp && <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> <a href={whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener">write to us on WhatsApp</a>.</li>}
    {email && <li><strong>E-mail:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</li>}
    <li>
      <strong>The quiz on our home page:</strong> answer the <a href="/#quiz">four questions</a>, leave your name and
      WhatsApp number and tick the consent box. We’ll contact you on WhatsApp, and you can tell us there that your
      request is about your data. For such a request, your answers to the first three questions do not matter.
    </li>
  </ul>
  {!direct && (
    <p>
      As of {asOf}, the company has not yet published a phone number, WhatsApp number or e-mail address on this site,
      so the quiz is the one way to reach us through it. We answer every request about your data within one month, as
      the GDPR requires.
    </p>
  )}
  {direct && <p>We answer every request about your data within one month, as the GDPR requires.</p>}

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  {consent ? (
    <p>
      <strong>When you visit the website.</strong> The website is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). Like
      every web server, GitHub’s servers process your IP address and basic technical information about your request, such as
      your browser type, to deliver the page and keep the service secure. The website sets no cookies of its own and uses no
      analytics tools. It keeps one note in your browser’s storage: whether you accepted or declined cookies in the banner,
      so that it does not ask again on every page. {pixel && tags
        ? 'The advertising tools it can use are the Meta Pixel and the conversion tags of our advertisers, described next, and only if you accept them.'
        : pixel ? 'The one advertising tool it can use is the Meta Pixel, described next, and only if you accept it.'
        : 'The advertising tools it can use are the conversion tags of our advertisers, described next, and only if you accept them.'}
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      <strong>When you visit the website.</strong> The website is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). It sets
      no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and uses no analytics, advertising or tracking tools. Like every web server,
      GitHub’s servers process your IP address and basic technical information about your request, such as your browser
      type, to deliver the page and keep the service secure.
    </p>
  )}
  {pixel && (
    <>
      <p id="meta-pixel">
        <strong>The Meta Pixel, only if you accept it.</strong> When you open the website, a banner asks whether we may use the
        Meta Pixel, a tool of Meta Platforms Ireland Ltd. (the company behind Facebook and Instagram). Until you press Accept,
        nothing from Meta is loaded. If you accept, your browser loads the pixel from Meta’s servers (connect.facebook.net);
        it sets cookies such as <code>_fbp</code> and sends Meta the address of each page you open, your IP address and
        information about your browser and device, and, on the page you see after sending the quiz, the fact that a request
        was sent. Your answers, your name and your WhatsApp number are never sent to Meta. If you have a Facebook or
        Instagram account, Meta can link this to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use it to see which visits and requests come from our adverts on Instagram and Facebook, and to improve who those
        adverts are shown to. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR, and the Belgian rules on cookies). We
        and Meta are jointly responsible for collecting this data and sending it to Meta; what Meta does with it afterwards
        is Meta’s own responsibility, as described in <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta’s privacy policy</a>.
        Meta may process it outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States. If you press Decline,
        nothing from Meta is loaded, on any page.
      </p>
    </>
  )}
  {tags && (
    <p id="conversion-tags">
      <strong>Our advertisers’ conversion tags, only if you accept them.</strong> After you accept cookies in the banner, the
      page you see after sending the quiz may load the conversion tags of the advertising services we use, to tell them that
      a request was sent; these services may set their own cookies. If you press Decline, none of these tags is loaded.
    </p>
  )}
  {consent && (
    <p>
      You can change your choice at any time{pixel ? '; declining later also removes the Meta Pixel’s cookies from this website' : ''}.
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm ck-change" data-cookie-change hidden>{site.cookies.change}</button>
    </p>
  )}

  <Content />
</LegalPage>

<style>
  .ck-change { display: flex; margin-block-start: 0.8rem; }
  .ck-change[hidden] { display: none; }
</style>
